  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "minimal house: the four, a clicky cross-stick and a shaker placed sparingly and swung a little, an offbeat hat, and a sub of short bouncing notes",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars. The house's own outline with the parts taken out and the few that stay made to talk: a cross-stick on the a of one, the e of three and the and of four in the first bar, two in the second; a shaker on four sixteenths only; the closed hat on each and; a sub that bounces on the and of one and the a of two. Swung 0.54."
  }
